John,

Attached is a first draft. I started from the consulting-services
template I use for a couple of other technology clients and built it
around the terms memo you sent over on the 23rd, so most of what you
and Alice already agreed should be in there in something close to your
own words.

A few things I want you to look at before this goes anywhere near your
customer.

1. Response time and after-hours language. I put it in almost exactly
as you wrote it. That's unusual -- most of my clients want to promise
more than they can deliver and I spend my time talking them out of it.
You've done the opposite. I left it alone.

2. Termination. Your memo didn't say anything about how either side
gets out of the monthly arrangement, so I left the notice period blank
in Section 11 rather than guess. You and Alice should decide what you
actually want there before I treat this as final; it's the kind of
number a customer's lawyer will have an opinion about. Same for the
liability cap in Section 8: I'd normally put a number in, but it's your
exposure and you should pick it.

3. Insurance. You are about to take on contractual responsibility for
somebody else's production revenue systems. I put a placeholder clause
in at Section 9 requiring general liability and, ideally, a technology
E&O / professional liability policy, but I don't know whether you have
either one yet. If you don't, get a quote before you sign this, not
after. I'm not your broker, but I can give you the name of the person
who wrote the policy for two of my other clients if that's useful.

4. Entity details. I've bracketed your side of the signature page and
the recitals. Send me the exact registered name, the entity type and
who signs for it, and I'll fill those in.

My time on this draft is inside the flat $750 we discussed for a first
set of company documents. A second round of substantive changes -- not
typos, actual changes -- is $185/hour, so it's worth getting your and
Alice's comments consolidated before you send anything back to me.

Happy to talk through any of this by phone before it goes to your
customer.

